1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,380
The dogs ran straight for the tanks...

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:04,520
just as they were trained.

3
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:07,040
But these were Soviet dogs.

4
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:08,790
And so were the tanks.

5
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:10,570
1941.

6
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:13,580
German tanks were tearing into the Soviet Union.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,060
For years, trainers kept the dogs hungry,

8
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,020
and hid their food under tanks.

9
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,630
A tank meant dinner.

10
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:23,670
Now each dog wore explosives, with a wooden lever on its back.

11
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:26,090
Under a tank, the lever hit the steel.

12
00:00:26,110 --> 00:00:28,060
But they had trained on Soviet tanks:

13
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:30,550
silent, still, smelling of diesel.

14
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:33,840
German tanks roared, fired, and smelled strange.

15
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:36,400
Some dogs ran for the tanks they knew.

16
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:40,120
Of the first 30 dogs, only 4 reached a German tank.

17
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:42,650
Others fled back to their own trenches...

18
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,920
still carrying their bombs.

19
00:00:45,610 --> 00:00:48,440
Moscow later claimed 300 tanks.

20
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:50,150
Historians doubt it.

21
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:52,410
Because out there, in the smoke and noise,

22
00:00:52,430 --> 00:00:54,080
hungry and terrified...

